<article class="env-lemma" id="0EV3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EV3">Lemma <span data-tag="0EV3">38.35.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in a big site $\mathit{Sch}_ h$. Let $F : (\mathit{Sch}/S)_ h^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$ be an h sheaf satisfying property (b) of Topologies, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EUW" data-tag="0EUW">34.13.1</a> with $\mathcal{C} = (\mathit{Sch}/S)_ h$. Then the extension $F'$ of $F$ to the category of all schemes over $S$ satisfies the sheaf condition for all h coverings and is limit preserving (Limits, Remark <a href="/tag/05LX" data-tag="05LX">32.6.2</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is proven by the arguments given in the proofs of Topologies, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0GDW" data-tag="0GDW">34.13.3</a> and <a href="/tag/0EUX" data-tag="0EUX">34.13.4</a> using Lemmas <a href="/tag/0EV2" data-tag="0EV2">38.35.3</a> and <a href="/tag/0EU0" data-tag="0EU0">38.34.12</a>. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>